  "draft_text": "The appellant relies on Asha Devi v. Ravi Kumar, (2091) 4 SCC 210, para 12, where the Court held that “Joint possession of one co-sharer is in law possession of all co-sharers, unless ouster is pleaded and proved.” The respondent's reliance on Imaginary Lal v. Fictional Devi, (2099) 9 SCC 999 is misplaced. In Asha Devi (2091) 4 SCC 210 the Court also said that “Joint possession of one co-sharer is in law possession of every co-sharer.” The old view in Old Holding v. State, (2080) 1 SCC 5 no longer governs. Section 4 of the Model Partition Act, 2091 requires valuation, but section 99 of the Model Partition Act, 2091 is also invoked. See also the firm's note CF-MEMO-7 and Future Bench v. Union, (2092) 2 SCC 50.",
  "note": "Generated by certificate::tests with a fixed TEST seed ([42; 32]) and time. Never a real install key."
